  "fit": "per admitted scan batch, world and noise model, the least chi-square of the batch's three contrasts over the world's one parameter, at the retention or noise strength that reproduces the center arm's visibility through the mean assignment matrix of the two brackets; the noise models are 13 contraction shares (the part of the visibility loss that depolarizes the data bits alone, 0 to 1) and the gate-noise families cz_depolarizing, pulse_dephasing, cz_dephasing, cz_damping, damping_and_dephasing; a world's chi-square is the sum over the admitted scan batches at the one noise model that makes the sum least",
  "guard": "a data batch is admitted when e01 and e10 of each qubit the statistics read (d0, d1, the selector and the coin) change by at most 0.02 between the readout batch before it and the one after; d2 is summed out of both statistics and its qubit's rates are reported unguarded; the decision needs at least one admitted batch of every scan kind, otherwise it reads unresolved_guard",
  "qx": "every circuit within twice the sampling floor of its ideal law"
